-field-d3261e01-b350-524c-a353-a2dfc7e7e037" :answer-field/choices "answer-a52a1264-daf9-5585-a899-ca4955b26a0c"] ["answer-field-d3261e01-b350-524c-a353-a2dfc7e7e037" :answer-field/choices "answer-fae94e29-660b-5543-bab0-87e8d67f1ae2"] ["answer-field-d3261e01-b350-524c-a353-a2dfc7e7e037" :answer-field/choices "answer-b2b08043-54bd-579b-a710-49e36d027167"] ["question-28327fac-a614-5756-91bd-3fcab54fcda2" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-d3261e01-b350-524c-a353-a2dfc7e7e037"] [17592186124637 :knowledge-point/questions "question-28327fac-a614-5756-91bd-3fcab54fcda2"] ["question-f90f5dc8-4e9d-5e87-800a-708d8b32cd8d" :question/id #uuid "f90f5dc8-4e9d-5e87-800a-708d8b32cd8d"] ["question-f90f5dc8-4e9d-5e87-800a-708d8b32cd8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-158196"] ["question-f90f5dc8-4e9d-5e87-800a-708d8b32cd8d" :question/problem "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $g(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}?$"] ["question-f90f5dc8-4e9d-5e87-800a-708d8b32cd8d" :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1\\ge 0\n$$\n\nSince the inequality ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1\\ge 0$ is true for all values of $x$ and $y,$ the domain of the function $f$ is the entire $xy$-plane.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](images/40/402d90507403eabf4cd35cde83a45c9fa2d8080347e1debb0e2463be408b489b.png)"] ["question-f90f5dc8-4e9d-5e87-800a-708d8b32cd8d" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-b0c62e6a-7044-5e8e-b3aa-7123ad96f32d" :answer-field/id #uuid "b0c62e6a-7044-5e8e-b3aa-7123ad96f32d"] ["answer-e69db1ea-c330-5536-8560-08f5b1e80164" :answer/id #uuid "e69db1ea-c330-5536-8560-08f5b1e80164"] ["answer-e69db1ea-c330-5536-8560-08f5b1e80164" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-e69db1ea